From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] virtio_balloon: flush dirty pages when inflation stalls

0003's drop-caches-on-stall only drops *clean* cache. A guest doing
writes holds tens of MiB of dirty pagecache that can never be dropped
until writeback completes - inflation stalls with that memory stranded
on the host (the classic "guest uses 30 MiB, host shows 130 MiB" gap
when the rest is dirty + clean cache).

Extend the stall path in fill_balloon():

- on the first stalled allocation, wake the flusher threads
  (WB_REASON_VMSCAN, same reason vmscan uses) so dirty pages start
  cleaning, then drop clean cache/slab and retry,
- on the second stall, sleep ~1ms (usleep_range) to let that writeback complete,
  drop again and retry once more before giving up the batch,
- retry sleeps 20ms/10ms -> ~1ms usleep_range (12x faster at HZ=250,
  where msleep(10) is really 12ms); the outer update_balloon_size work
  requeues until diff==0, so yielding fast and retrying beats sleeping.

Only dirty data is flushed; clean data is dropped as before. Needs
<linux/writeback.h> for wakeup_flusher_threads().

Signed-off-by: openworld-kernel <noreply@openworld>
---
 drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c b/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
index 123456789022..123456789023 100644
--- a/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
+++ b/drivers/virtio/virtio_balloon.c
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
 #include <uapi/linux/virtio_ring.h>
 #include <linux/virtio_balloon.h>
 #include <linux/swap.h>
+#include <linux/writeback.h>
 #include <linux/workqueue.h>
 #include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/slab.h>
@@ -261,11 +262,25 @@
 
 		if (!page) {
 			/*
-			 * Aggressive last resort: drop all clean pagecache and
-			 * reclaimable slab system-wide, then retry once. This
-			 * converts cached memory into balloonable memory in one
-			 * shot instead of grinding it out via per-page reclaim.
+			 * Dirty pages can never be ballooned directly - kick
+			 * writeback so they become clean and droppable, then
+			 * drop all clean pagecache and reclaimable slab
+			 * system-wide and retry. Without the flush a
+			 * dirty-heavy guest stalls here with tens of MiB
+			 * stranded on the host.
 			 */
+			wakeup_flusher_threads(WB_REASON_VMSCAN);
+			balloon_drop_caches();
+			page = balloon_page_alloc();
+		}
+
+		if (!page) {
+			/*
+			 * Second chance: the writeback kicked above may have
+			 * completed - drop again and retry once before
+			 * giving up the batch.
+			 */
+			usleep_range(500, 1500);
 			balloon_drop_caches();
 			page = balloon_page_alloc();
 		}
@@ -278,7 +293,7 @@
 			 * Aggressive: retry quickly so large inflates converge
 			 * faster under pressure (outer work requeues on diff).
 			 */
-			msleep(20);
+			usleep_range(500, 1500);
 			break;
 		}
 

